#: ../../../system/hexagon/sdk-programs.rst:23
msgid "SDK programs and semihosting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/sdk-programs.rst:25
msgid ""
"The simulator-compatible machines, such as ``V66G_1024`` and ``V68N_1024``, "
"provide semihosting by default. The SDK runtime uses ``trap0`` calls for "
"services such as console I/O, host file access, and program termination."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/sdk-programs.rst:30
msgid "See :ref:`hexagon-semihosting` for more info."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/sdk-programs.rst:32
msgid "The examples below use v68 SDK artifacts with ``-M V68N_1024``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/sdk-programs.rst:35
msgid "Standalone OS programs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/sdk-programs.rst:37
msgid ""
"By default, ``hexagon-clang`` links a bare-metal executable with the SDK's "
"standalone OS startup code and C runtime. This small runtime initializes the "
"machine, calls ``main()``, and implements hosted services through "
"semihosting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/sdk-programs.rst:42
msgid "For example, save the following as ``prog.c``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/sdk-programs.rst:44
msgid ""
"#include <stdio.h>\n"
"\n"
"int main(int argc, char **argv)\n"
"{\n"
"    for (int i = 0; i < argc; i++) {\n"
"        printf(\"argv[%d] = %s\\n\", i, argv[i]);\n"
"    }\n"
"    return 0;\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/sdk-programs.rst:56
msgid "With the SDK tools on ``PATH``, build and run it with:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/sdk-programs.rst:58
msgid ""
"hexagon-clang -mv68 prog.c -o prog.elf\n"
"qemu-system-hexagon -M V68N_1024 -display none \\\n"
"    -kernel ./prog.elf -append \"foo bar\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/sdk-programs.rst:64
msgid "The program prints:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/sdk-programs.rst:66
msgid ""
"argv[0] = ./prog.elf\n"
"argv[1] = foo\n"
"argv[2] = bar"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/sdk-programs.rst:73
msgid "Guest command-line arguments"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/sdk-programs.rst:75
msgid ""
"The example above passes the arguments with ``-append``. QEMU uses the ``-"
"kernel`` filename as the first semihosting argument and splits ``-append`` "
"on spaces to supply the remaining arguments. The host shell quotes keep "
"``foo bar`` together as the value of the QEMU option; the guest runtime "
"subsequently parses the semihosting command line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/sdk-programs.rst:81
msgid ""
"You can instead specify the semihosting command line with ``arg=`` options:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/sdk-programs.rst:83
msgid ""
"qemu-system-hexagon -M V68N_1024 -display none -kernel ./prog.elf \\\n"
"    -semihosting-config 'enable=on,target=native,arg=./"
"prog.elf,arg=foo,arg=bar'"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/sdk-programs.rst:88
msgid "Include the program name as the first ``arg=`` value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/sdk-programs.rst:90
msgid ""
"``target=native`` selects QEMU's implementation of semihosting even when a "
"debugger is connected. To connect the semihosting console explicitly to the "
"terminal, add a character device and select it with ``chardev=``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/sdk-programs.rst:94
msgid ""
"qemu-system-hexagon -M V68N_1024 -display none \\\n"
"    -chardev stdio,id=semi \\\n"
"    -semihosting-config enable=on,target=native,chardev=semi \\\n"
"    -kernel ./prog.elf -append \"foo bar\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/sdk-programs.rst:102
msgid "QuRT programs and the SDK loader chain"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/sdk-programs.rst:104
msgid "An SDK QuRT dynamic test consists of three guest images:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/sdk-programs.rst:106
msgid "``runelf.pbn`` boots QuRT and loads a user process from a host file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/sdk-programs.rst:107
msgid ""
"``run_main_on_hexagon_sim`` is that process. It initializes the dynamic "
"loader and loads the application's shared object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/sdk-programs.rst:109
msgid ""
"``userprog.so`` exports ``main(int argc, char **argv)``, which the runner "
"invokes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/sdk-programs.rst:112
msgid ""
"QEMU initially loads only ``runelf.pbn``. The subsequent stages read the "
"other images through semihosting. Use matching SDK architecture variants for "
"the boot image, runner, and application. For example, with Hexagon SDK 6.4 "
"and its toolv19 v68 artifacts:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/sdk-programs.rst:117
msgid ""
"runelf=\"$HEXAGON_SDK_ROOT/rtos/qurt/computev68/sdksim_bin/runelf.pbn\"\n"
"runner=\"$HEXAGON_SDK_ROOT/libs/run_main_on_hexagon/ship/hexagon_toolv19_v68/"
"run_main_on_hexagon_sim\"\n"
"qemu-system-hexagon -M V68N_1024 -display none \\\n"
"    -kernel \"$runelf\" -append \"$runner -- ./userprog.so foo bar\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/sdk-programs.rst:124
msgid ""
"Build ``userprog.so`` with the SDK's QuRT shared-library build rules, "
"including any libraries needed by the application, and place its shared "
"dependencies where the SDK dynamic loader can find them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/sdk-programs.rst:128
msgid "The command line exposed through semihosting is:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/sdk-programs.rst:130
msgid "<runelf.pbn path> <runner path> -- ./userprog.so foo bar"
msgstr ""

